with all things considered i think it's  safe to say that the summer anime season  came back with a vengeance from  action-packed series romantic ventures  heart-wrenching dramas and light-hearted  comedies  this season has it all for you i'm not  even gonna talk about the sequels we all  know that this season is rife with  sequels of popular shows but for an  extra challenge i won't be talking about  them here after all my point is to show  that the season is such a strong one in  its own right so strap your seat belts  on and get ready to be amazed by the  various offerings that the anime  industry has given us  this season  so to start things off we go with japan  sings 2020.  it's been a while since we've been  treated with a grim disaster series in  the same vein as tokyo magnitude 2.0  which i've talked about in an older  video that i'll link on the top of the  screen japan sings 2020 kicks off with  an earthquake of insane proportions  we've always known that eventually a  giant earthquake has the chance to wreck  japan  and this netflix series takes a look at  the possibility through the lens of the  country  literally finding its way into a watery  grave it is at its core  not exactly a disaster series because  the said disasters only  set the tone for the more important  cultural themes that surface overall i  think that for something marketed as a  disaster series japan sings 2020 is  all things considered a pretty nice and  gripping show it does have its  shortcomings though while there are lots  of interesting themes a lot of them do  feel underdeveloped nevertheless  when it comes to tone and music this one  is still pretty decent  [Music]  next we move on to fog hill of five  elements for our number nine entry  non-japanese anime have been slowly  making some headway now and one of those  that's currently airing is fog hill of  five elements four kill of five elements  while having just a decent  interesting premise truly shines in its  jaw-dropping animation  unique art style and overall flair it  looks unique and stands out from what  we've been used to seeing which helps  feed into the overall enjoyment in  watching the show i feel that it does  need a lot more love than what it's  getting right now but its current status  is understandable given the lack of a  proper translation and promotion in  mainstream avenues  don't sleep on this show though it's got  some really amazing fights which got  featured in a previous video by the way  that are sure to give a lot of japanese  anime a run for their money  up next at number eight we have  uzaki-chan wants to hang out  can't get enough of dagaki-san then we  might have the next best thing for you  a nice innocent slice-of-life show  uzaki-chan wants to hang out tells the  trials and tribulations of sakura  shinichi after all  what else do you call it when all you  want is a little bit of peace and quiet  but in comes the loud underclassmen who  seemingly make a living poking fun at  you perhaps all of this teasing will  lead to something else blossoming  between the two of them  only time will tell probably more known  for the in my opinion  unjustified controversy uzaki chant is  probably on a lot of your radars i find  it a shame that the controversy had to  take precedence because on its own the  show's really relaxing it's just a fun  watch all throughout it's not deep or  complex but it doesn't need to be i  don't get tired of the main character's  antics at all and they make it a really  enjoyable combination to watch  make sure to watch this if you really  want to unwind  [Music]  making its triumphant return now with a  full uninterrupted run  is apari ranman its premise is simple  yet adventurous  no pun intended there on one hand you  have the socially awkward apare  with the goal to travel across the world  through his numerous machines and  inventions  through some twists of fate he finds  himself stranded in america with his  trusty partner the samurai kosami  left with no money or plans the two take  part in a race across the continent  promising afari the chance to showcase  his inventions and kosamay the resources  to get back home  thus the partnership between two  unlikely allies is born the show which  is  basically steel ball run in 2020 gives  us a lot of things to like  its colourful and bizarre world are  things that showcase the creativity of  anime in general  i also find the interaction between the  many characters quite entertaining to  watch  it's definitely a show that you could  enjoy  [Music]  2020 seems to be a very good year for  overpowered protagonists mahogany's  coming back in the last quarter of the  year and we have the return of kirito in  this season  sword art online airing alongside  alicization is the show  featuring the third member of the trio  of overpowered light novel protagonists  that somewhat look alike misfit  at demon king academy anas voldigold is  many things with his godlike power  that's beyond comprehension and in his  confidence he allows himself to be  killed and reincarnated 2 000 years in  the future only to wake up to a future  where history has been rewritten  and no one recognizes his status as the  demon king  even the overall power level of the  world has fallen after years of peace  however everything's but a minor  inconvenience in the face of the demon  king  that's come to retake his throne after  two millennia the era  of magic school light novels has come  full circle here and now we have  something like the one punch man of the  genre misfit's just so over the top that  it's entertaining  even for someone who's not too fond of  this genre it's just crazy to think how  far we've come to be fair in between  all of the craziness featuring the  almighty and osama misfit is an  enjoyable show with its fair share of  drama and touching moments so it's way  more than just a parody of sorts  rent a girlfriend is our number five  entry  [Music]  after getting dumped by his girlfriend  kazuya attempts to make up and fill the  void in his heart by taking  advantage of the japan classic the  rental girlfriend getting the right one  to pretend to be your girlfriend's easy  and the pretty and caring chizuru seems  to be the perfect choice for him however  things don't go as planned and with the  two having quite a rough going on their  date it seems to be a partnership  destined to do things get even more  muddled when kazuya hears of his  grandmother's collapse  and gets forced to bring chizuru along  with him not wanting to break the heart  of his grandmother who becomes overjoyed  at kazuya finally finding a serious  girlfriend kazuya and chizuru get forced  into a fake relationship  to be fair compared to the usual  rom-coms the premise of this anime does  have a different execution and i think  that rent-a-girlfriends rightfully one  of the most trending shows this season  even beating out the sequels to popular  shows at this time the main character  does get his fair share of criticism but  the hijinks and the comedy keep me  coming back on this one probably check  the first few episodes of this and see  if it's your liking  a whisker away has been through a lot  thanks to the situation of the world at  large  what was supposed to be a film ready for  theatrical release ended up becoming a  netflix offer  sometime right before the summer season  a whisker away ends up being something  you'd expect from a disney movie  but with anime characters you know the  whimsical romantic story involving magic  and transformation that we've come to  know while the story might seem quite  plain at first i think that it ended up  quite nice and heartwarming the arts  just amazing and exceptional as expected  from a full-length anime film  a whisker away is no shingai movie but i  think that it's a dramatic and  heartwarming adventure that's a good way  to spend 2 hours of your time it's a  really fun story that you can settle  down and enjoy with the family  much of the joy of fangirls worldwide  millionaire detective has made its  glorious return and likely for good the  comedy show that follows the duo of the  hilariously rich daisuke and every man  detective haru has hit the ground  running once again  the main draw of the series for me  though is the chemistry between the main  duo the two  are polar opposites and their chemistry  helps make the show very fun to watch  now i know a lot of people who find dice  gay swag and riches hilarious mean  material and i dare say that his antics  helped push the charming story just to  the next level the humor is great  the action's nice and the characters are  just so over the top that the show just  becomes  so entertaining if you've not given the  show a try from the previous season  now's the time to join the ride  in second place we have god of high  school admittedly i underestimated the  fan base for god of high school before  the season came in  i knew it was going to be popular and  for good reason too but i didn't expect  it to blow up like this as early as the  first episode does it deserve the hype  hell yeah god of high school has by all  measures a simple plot and premise cocky  high schooler thinks he's hot stuff  gets his ass kicked and starts his  journey to win the king of the iron fist  tournament  hmm i mean the god of high school yes  that's the name of the tournament along  the way  expect to see some of the coolest and  most breathtaking fight scenes this  season has to offer the show made me a  believer so early with this amazing  fight choreography and animation and i  can't wait to see  what's gonna happen next in spite of all  these things as a webtoon reader myself  i was a bit disappointed with the pacing  and the content that was cut  but after the tower of god adaptation i  guess this is something we should have  expected one of the reasons why i listed  this show in second place is because if  you don't mind the simple plot and i  hear mainly for the action this show  would probably be my top pick of the  season for you  with so many candidates i think there's  only one show that i'm gonna vote for in  the top spot  and it's decadence  entering the season i wasn't completely  sure on what to make of decadence it  seemed to have this dystopian steampunk  flair going on for it and i think that a  couple of people penciled it in as  basically another attack on titan when  the first episode hit but  boy did the show prove everyone wrong i  think that what decadence does well is  to subvert the expectations  when you have a world where monsters  have wiped out most of the people you  immediately get those attack on titan  vibes but the anime has done a good job  of throwing the twists early the show  which is made by studio nut also looks  very stylish very trigger-like and has a  lot of action-packed scenes that you've  come to know this studio for from the  second episode onwards you can see that  the show's no longer the generic monster  versus humans post-apocalyptic show  everyone made it out to be  don't sleep on decadence i'm telling you  i think it's underrated for the amount  of creativity and passion that you can  see in this thing  see challenge mode of not talking about  the numerous sequels turned up pretty  high didn't it don't you think so among  the shows listed here  what are your favorites make sure to  tell me in the comment section below and  i'll gladly have a chat with you about  them looks like the season turned out a  lot better than we expected in march now  don't you think now i wonder which of  these shows will rise further and become  anime of the season for the community  only time will tell i guess now if you  haven't already make sure to hit that  sweet like and subscribe button and i'll  be waiting for you on the next video  see ya  you

